   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import hashlib, platform, json, warnings\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from scipy import stats, optimize\n",
    "from IPython.display import display, Markdown\n",
    "SEED = 640\n",
    "rng = np.random.default_rng(SEED)\n",
    "DATA_PATH = Path('Nifty500_Standalone_Quarterly_Available.csv')\n",
    "if not DATA_PATH.exists():\n",
    "    DATA_PATH = Path('outputs/nifty500_analysis') / DATA_PATH.name\n",
    "OUTPUT = DATA_PATH.parent / 'statistical_outputs'\n",
    "OUTPUT.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({'figure.figsize': (10, 5), 'axes.grid': True, 'figure.dpi': 110})\n",
    "raw = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH, low_memory=False)\n",
    "provenance = {'csv_sha256': hashlib.sha256(DATA_PATH.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n",
    "              'rows': len(raw), 'columns': len(raw.columns), 'python': platform.python_version(),\n",
    "              'pandas': pd.__version__, 'numpy': np.__version__, 'scipy': __import__('scipy').__version__}\n",
    "display(pd.Series(provenance, name='Reproducibility'))\n",
    "(OUTPUT/'provenance.json').write_text(json.dumps(provenance, indent=2))\n",
    "display(raw.head(3))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "59136419",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Statistical questions and hypotheses\n",
    "- RQ1: H0 is that PAT, revenue, finance costs, basic EPS and other-income slopes are jointly zero, conditional on industry and target-quarter controls.\n",
    "- RQ2: H0 is that each of the five specified financial slopes is zero. Apply Holm correction across the five coefficient tests.\n",
    "- Alpha is .05, with two-sided coefficient tests. Company clustering is primary conditional evidence; quarter clustering and two-way covariance are sensitivity calculations.\n",
    "- Predictive usefulness is distinct from association. No inference result here establishes that a forecasting model beats the historical baseline."
   ]
  },
