  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bf38dd5f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Feature engineering and consecutive-quarter target\n",
    "Quarter labels are calendar quarters, not Indian fiscal-quarter labels. An exact company-quarter join prevents a missing quarter from being treated as the next quarter. Reported predictors use current-quarter values. Ratios require strictly positive denominators. Financial Services are retained as a separate industry, with sector diagnostics; revenue-based ratios are less comparable across financial and nonfinancial companies.\n",
    "\n",
    "No generic operating-profit variable is fabricated from the banking-specific field. Sparse assets, equity and borrowings are omitted from the default model rather than synthesizing ROA/ROE/debt-to-equity from unsupported values."
   ]
  },
