   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "CR1 mean-variance and Holm adjustment checks passed.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from itertools import combinations, product\n",
    "ALPHA = .05\n",
    "STATS_OUTPUT = OUTPUT / 'statistical_tests'\n",
    "STATS_OUTPUT.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "def holm_adjust(pvalues):\n",
    "    p = np.asarray(pvalues, dtype=float)\n",
    "    answer = np.full(len(p), np.nan)\n",
    "    good = np.flatnonzero(np.isfinite(p))\n",
    "    order = good[np.argsort(p[good])]\n",
    "    # Family size includes unavailable planned tests; conservative if some fail.\n",
    "    if len(order):\n",
    "        answer[order] = np.minimum(1, np.maximum.accumulate((len(p)-np.arange(len(order)))*p[order]))\n",
    "    return answer\n",
    "\n",
    "def cluster_covariance(X, residual, groups):\n",
    "    \"\"\"CR1 sandwich: G/(G-1)*(N-1)/(N-K)*bread*cluster_meat*bread.\"\"\"\n",
    "    X = np.asarray(X, float); residual = np.asarray(residual, float)\n",
    "    codes, levels = pd.factorize(np.asarray(groups))\n",
    "    assert (codes >= 0).all(), 'Missing cluster identifier'\n",
    "    N,K = X.shape; G = len(levels)\n",
    "    if G < 2 or N <= K: raise ValueError('Too few clusters or residual degrees of freedom')\n",
    "    score = np.zeros((G,K))\n",
    "    np.add.at(score, codes, X*residual[:,None])\n",
    "    bread = np.linalg.inv(X.T@X)\n",
    "    cov = (G/(G-1))*((N-1)/(N-K))*(bread@(score.T@score)@bread)\n",
    "    return (cov+cov.T)/2, G\n",
    "\n",
    "def coefficient_table(beta, cov, df, names):\n",
    "    variance = np.diag(cov)\n",
    "    se = np.sqrt(np.where(variance>0,variance,np.nan))\n",
    "    t = beta/se; crit = stats.t.ppf(.975,df)\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame({'term':names,'coefficient':beta,'SE':se,'t':t,\n",
    "        'df':df,'p':2*stats.t.sf(np.abs(t),df),\n",
    "        'CI95_lower':beta-crit*se,'CI95_upper':beta+crit*se})\n",
    "\n",
    "def joint_wald(beta, cov, indices, df):\n",
    "    b=beta[indices]; v=cov[np.ix_(indices,indices)]; q=len(indices)\n",
    "    eig=np.linalg.eigvalsh(v)\n",
    "    if eig.min() <= max(1e-12, eig.max()*1e-10):\n",
    "        return {'F':np.nan,'df1':q,'df2':df,'p':np.nan,'status':'Singular or nonpositive restricted covariance'}\n",
    "    F=float(b@np.linalg.solve(v,b)/q)\n",
    "    return {'F':F,'df1':q,'df2':df,'p':stats.f.sf(F,q,df),'status':'Computed; cluster asymptotic approximation'}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Numerical cross-check: a one-observation-per-cluster intercept model equals the usual mean t test.\n",
    "check=np.array([1.,2.,4.,8.,10.]); check_X=np.ones((len(check),1))\n",
    "check_cov,_=cluster_covariance(check_X,check-check.mean(),np.arange(len(check)))\n",
    "assert np.isclose(check_cov[0,0],check.var(ddof=1)/len(check))\n",
    "assert np.isclose(holm_adjust([.01,.04,.03]),[.03,.06,.06]).all()\n",
    "print('CR1 mean-variance and Holm adjustment checks passed.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "38cc6a0b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## RQ1 and RQ2: interpretable statistical regression\n",
    "Use five reported predictors chosen for accounting meaning: PAT, revenue, finance costs, basic EPS and other income. Complete-case development observations are used; inference does not treat median-imputed values as observed measurements. Each predictor is transformed using signed `log1p(abs(x))` and standardized within this inferential sample. Include industry and target-quarter fixed effects to control average industry and period differences. This is a pooled association model; it is not a firm fixed-effects causal model. The target remains untrimmed PAT growth in percentage points.\n",
    "\n",
    "Five standardized slopes are jointly tested for RQ1. RQ2 reports company-clustered t tests, unadjusted 95% CIs, and Holm-adjusted p-values over the five slopes. Intervals are pointwise, not simultaneous. Quarter-cluster and two-way results are sensitivity estimates. Sector/quarter controls are nuisance terms, not part of the five-slope financial test. The robust Wald F is distinct from the conventional homoskedastic OLS F-test.\n",
    "\n",
    "The CR1 formula follows the cluster sandwich covariance documented by statsmodels. It is implemented transparently with NumPy/SciPy so no additional package installation is needed: https://www.statsmodels.org/stable/generated/statsmodels.stats.sandwich_covariance.cov_cluster.html"
   ]
  },
