   "source": [
    "## Regression diagnostics\n",
    "VIF measures predictor collinearity conditional on the other design columns. The residual Q–Q plot, fitted-versus-residual plot and skewness/kurtosis describe departures from conventional OLS assumptions. A Breusch–Pagan LM test against the five financial predictors is included as an **iid diagnostic reference only**: its conventional p-value is not panel-robust. It does not determine whether to switch covariance estimators after seeing the result. Cluster-robust covariance is used throughout. Company-cluster robust tests still require adequate independent clusters and model specification; few time clusters and extreme target values remain material limitations."
   ]
  },
